# 5b piece 4 — mutations M31…M42 against GREEN 970df5b (AC-312; D-116 F-7 A, D-124 F-21 B)
# Each mutation breaks ONE rule, rebuilds, runs: swift test --skip-build --filter 'MLXResidency|MLXPrewarmOrderTests'
# then reverts with git checkout. This Mac: macOS 26.6.1, Xcode 27, Swift 6.4; no warnings-as-errors.
#
# FIRST RUN — read it with these corrections:
#  * M32 (a cancel answers nothing) HUNG: the waiter stayed parked for ever, and the test helper waited on it
#    inside a task group, so the run passed its one-minute limit and did not end. It was KILLED BY HAND after
#    about three minutes. The runner then printed 'SURVIVED (masked)' because the killed process had printed
#    no failure line — THAT LINE IS WRONG: a test that never finishes is red. The helper was the weakness.
#  * M42 (waits when nothing is on its way) was killed by the one-minute time limit (64 s), not by a check.
#  * M40 (the catch path of ensureModelLoaded) SURVIVED, as expected: without weights or the shader library the
#    door refuses before a load begins, so no row on this Mac reaches it. Documented beside the line.
#  * M35 (startPrewarm's riding ask not lowered) was NOT RUN: it needs a warm that cannot finish while a second
#    prewarm arrives, and only real weights give that deterministically.
# FIX: the helper now races the waiter with two unstructured tasks (test support), and every scripted
# whenWarm() goes through it — a waiter nobody answers fails its row in 10 s.
# SECOND RUN (M32 and M42 alone, with the fixed helper): both KILLED in about 10 s.
# RESULT: 7 of 8 run mutations killed; M40 survives by design of this Mac; M35 not run.

